# The calibration mask: the fields on which two replays of one sequence on one target
# differ, so that no comparison can read them. One mask to a line, sorted by field:
#
#   <field> <cause> <issue>
#
# The causes are unsettled (the application is still working when the reply is written and
# shows nothing to wait on), clock (the value follows the time) and environment (the value
# follows the machine). A mask grows only when two GTK replays of a seed differ, and the
# line above it says what the differential mode can no longer see. Every fuzz summary
# prints how many there are. See docs/testing.md, "Calibration".
